      "math_academy_id": "q-70399",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1,1)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x-4)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x-4)$ is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $4$ units to the *right*. So the $y$-coordinate remains unchanged while the $x$-coordinate increases by $4.$\n\nWe know that the point $(1,1)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1+4,1)=(5,1)$ must lie on $y=f(x-4).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14214993/assets/8c736b4ad424cfc7efe3cd7218f873655b5bface8fe4cc670b8185ff1b73f5e5.png)",
